  "description": "NELZUA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C42 H72 Cu6 Dy3 F18 N6 O27 3+,2(Cl1 1-),Cl1 O4 1-,4.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu5 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu6 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.139-3.820 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 82.62-114.51°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [DyIII3CuII6L6(μ3-OH)6(H2O)10]Cl2·ClO4·3.5H2O (C42H81Cl3Cu6Dy3F18N6O35.50). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III), Cu(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
